<title>SWEDEN: Trelleborg unit buys Canada firms.</title>
<headline>Trelleborg unit buys Canada firms.</headline>
<dateline>STOCKHOLM 1996-11-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>Swedish metals and mining group Trelleborg said on Thursday its U.S. subsidiary Goodall had bought parts of Canadian distribution companies Snowden Rubber and Anderson CP Rubber from Canada's Starcan Corporation.  </p>
<p>The purchased companies have 17 sales offices throughout Canada for the distribution of industrial rubber items with combined turnover of around $40 million.</p>
<p>-- Stockholm newsroom +46-8-700-1004</p>
</text>
